.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt EMACS-DOCS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-docs
.Nd Static site for the Jotain Emacs configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm just
.Op Cm build | test | serve | ds-sync
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The site presents the Emacs configuration in
.Pa etc/emacs
as a landing page and a set of generated references.
The landing page looks like an Emacs frame.
It has a tab bar with three buffers, a mode line, and an
.Ql I-search
minibuffer over the sections of the page.
The design uses the Jylhis design system.
.Pp
The committed
.Pa public/
directory holds only the landing page, the shared CSS and JavaScript,
and the vendored design assets.
The Nix build in
.Pa package.nix
adds the generated content.
.Pp
The generated content is:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /docs/
Each
.Pa docs/**/*.mdx
page of
.Pa etc/emacs ,
ordered by
.Pa docs/docs.json .
.It Pa /manual/
The Info manual as HTML, and as
.Pa emacs-config.info .
.It Pa /man/
.Xr emacs-config 7
and the manual pages of the Emacs build.
.It Pa /info/emacs/ , Pa /info/elisp/
The GNU Emacs and Emacs Lisp manuals of the Emacs revision that the
configuration builds.
.It Pa /options/
The Nix module option reference.
.It Pa /help/packages/
The reference for each package, from the
.Ql ;;; @doc
markers in the Lisp files.
.It Pa /help/api/
The docstring reference for each bundled package.
.It Pa /packages/
Search over
.Pa /help/api/ .
.El
.Pp
The package omits
.Pa /help/api/
and
.Pa /packages/ .
Its
.Ql withApiDoc
attribute is the full site, which ingests the third-party API reference.
The
.Va baseHref
argument of
.Pa site.nix
prefixes every internal absolute URL.
Its default is the empty string, because the site is served from the root of
docs.example.org.
Pass a path such as
.Pa /docs
to serve it under a sub-path.
.Sh COMMANDS
Run these commands in this directory.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic just build
Build the site into
.Pa result/public .
This build documents Emacs and the configuration only.
It does not include the third-party API reference under
.Pa /help/api/
or the
.Pa /packages/
search.
.It Ic just test
Build the site and run the
.Ql ds-in-sync
check.
.It Ic just serve
Build the full site, with the API reference, and serve it at
.Pa http://localhost:8080/ .
.It Ic just deploy
Build the full site, with the API reference, with Nix and run
.Ql wrangler deploy
with the build result as the assets directory.
Needs
.Ev CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
and
.Ev CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID .
.It Ic just ds-sync
Copy the design assets of the in-tree design system
.Pq Pa lib/design
into
.Pa public/ds .
The package reads the committed copy.
Run it when the
.Ql ds-in-sync
check fails.
.El
.Pp
The Nix attributes are
.Ql local.packages.emacs-docs ,
.Ql local.checks.emacs-docs-build ,
and
.Ql local.checks.emacs-docs-ds-in-sync .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa package.nix
Builds the site and the checks.
It takes the Emacs sources from
.Pa ../../../etc/emacs
by path.
.It Pa site.nix
Assembles the site from
.Pa public/
and the generated references.
.It Pa public/
The deployed shell.
.It Pa public/ds/
Design system CSS and self-hosted fonts.
Never edit these files.
.It Pa wrangler.jsonc
The assets-only Worker that serves the site.
Its
.Va assets.directory
is the committed shell for local use;
the deploy overrides it with the Nix build result.
.El
.Sh CONVENTIONS
.Bl -bullet
.It
No hex literals in
.Pa public/css/site.css .
Colors come from the custom properties in
.Pa public/ds/tokens.css ,
so both modes stay in step.
.It
Some places cannot use a custom property and hold copies of token values:
the
.Ql theme-color
meta elements in
.Pa public/index.html ,
the page template in
.Pa site.nix ,
and
.Pa public/favicon.svg .
Update all of them when the theme changes.
.It
The style sheets for generated markup pin the heading elements to the
mono font.
An unstyled heading would use the large display face of the design system.
.It
Print (light) is the
.Ql :root
mode.
Negative (dark) is
.Ql data-mode="dark"
on the
.Ql html
element.
.It
The fonts are self-hosted.
The site makes no third-party requests.
.El
.Sh DEPLOYMENT
A push-mode static site, served at
.Lk https://docs.example.org
from the root.
Cloudflare Workers Builds has no Nix, so it cannot build the generated pages;
see
.Xr jylhis-deployment-model 7 .
Instead
.Pa .github/workflows/emacs-docs.yml
builds the full site with Nix on every push and pull request that touches
the site, the Emacs configuration or the design system.
On green
.Ql main
it copies the
.Pa public/
directory of the
.Ql packages.x86_64-linux.emacs-docs
result and runs
.Ql wrangler deploy --assets
for the
.Ql emacs-docs
Worker.
The job needs the
.Ev CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
and
.Ev CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
repository secrets.
The workflow's existence makes the generic
.Pa .github/workflows/sites.yml
skip this project.
.Pp
The
.Ql requires.dns
entry in
.Pa project.nix
makes the infra engine
.Pq Xr jylhis-infra-engine 7
bind
.Ql docs.example.org
to the Worker as a Workers custom domain.
Apply the infra plan before the first deploy.
.Pp
The old GitHub Pages site at jylhis.github.io/jotain (page.jylhis.com/jotain) should redirect to
docs.example.org once this site is live.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr emacs-config 7 ,
.Xr jylhis-deploying-static-sites 7 ,
.Xr jylhis-deployment-model 7 ,
.Xr jylhis-manual 7
.Sh HISTORY
The site started inside the Emacs configuration repository and was served
by GitHub Pages at page.jylhis.com/jotain.
It moved to this project with the configuration.
